Mechanical Energy - Basic Overview,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VrLVUfB_t_U,Explains mechanical energy as the sum of kinetic and potential energy and the conditions under which it is conserved.
Hooke's Law and Elastic Potential Energy,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OmMIOZtM1ks,Introduces Hooke's law and explains how to calculate elastic potential energy and the work required to stretch a spring.
How To Calculate The Work Required To Compress a Spring,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H5fiVnbHIf4,Explains how to calculate the work required to compress a spring.
What Is The Difference Between Work and Energy?,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x5mJRp8f6Ok,"Distinguishes work from energy and discusses internal energy, heat, work, and the action of forces."
Conservation of Energy Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_DwG8fukuj4,"Works through conservation-of-energy problems involving friction, inclined planes, and springs."
Projectile Motion and Conservation of Energy - College Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DFNTKiOB7t0,Solves projectile-motion problems using both conservation of energy and kinematic equations.
What is a Kilowatt hour?,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4BXZuQyAtIA,"Explains the kilowatt-hour as a unit of energy, converts it to megajoules, and calculates electricity costs for household appliances."
"Dot Product Formula of Power, Force, and Velocity",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WSP07nOjDvo,Explains how to calculate instantaneous power from force and velocity vectors using the dot product.
"Introduction to Momentum, Force, Newton's Second Law, Conservation of Linear Momentum, Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NIVNfI0RN2k,"Introduces momentum as mass times velocity, relates force to the rate of momentum change, derives momentum conservation from Newton's laws, and applies these ideas to a fluid jet."
Introduction to Impulse & Momentum - Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hODlmGK7pl8,"Introduces impulse and momentum, the impulse-momentum theorem, and Newton's second-law definition of force."
Conservation of Momentum Physics Problems - Basic Introduction,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fp7D5D8Bqjc,"Works through momentum-conservation problems involving an astronaut throwing a ball, an object breaking into fragments, and a load dropped into a railroad car."
Rocket Propulsion Physics & Mass Flow Rate - Newton's 3rd Law of Motion,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kvAf-Xouj8s,Explains rocket propulsion using Newton's third law and calculates thrust from exhaust velocity and mass flow rate.
Physics - What Really Is a Force?,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mril0zFVJXQ,Defines force in terms of momentum change and energy transfer.
Inelastic Collision Physics Problems In One Dimension - Conservation of Momentum,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C1XuwHLacao,"Solves one-dimensional inelastic-collision problems involving objects that stick together and a bullet embedding in a block, using momentum and energy conservation."
Impulse Momentum Theorem Physics Problems - Average Force & Contact Time,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1WIECGg71WY,"Explains the impulse-momentum theorem and calculates impulse, momentum change, final speed, average force, and contact time."
Force Time Graphs & Impulse - Physics Practice Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bv9ry123zck,Explains how to calculate impulse as the area under a force-time graph.

